Modifications made in Cachety (from 2026-10-10), relative to Filigrane Local:
  - Renamed and rebranded as Cachety (cachety.com); international default
    language (English) alongside French, Spanish, Arabic, Persian, Japanese
    and Chinese, with right-to-left layout for Arabic and Persian.
  - Guided help tour for first-time visitors, and an optional donation link.
  - Fact-checked comparison pages with other watermark tools (lib/compare).
  - New website around the tool: landing sections, privacy page, and
    practical guides per country (lib/guides, lib/site-copy.ts).
  - Mobile layout improvements (collapsible templates, one step per screen on phones).
  - Per-page Content-Security-Policy generation (one rule per page, within
    Cloudflare Pages limits), JSON-LD structured data and generated sitemap.
  - Continuous deployment to Cloudflare Pages from GitHub Actions.
  - Documentation translated to English and updated.
  - Simplified three-step tool (2026-10): guided watermark text with an
    editable full text ({recipient}, {date}, {code}), preview tools, sending
    options next to Download, done screen; easy-to-read 12-word passwords;
    public roadmap page (ROADMAP.md, lib/roadmap).
  - Security and feature work (file password, masking, traceable copies,
    several recipients, size budget, HEIC support, hardened headers and
    tests); see the git history for details.

